body:
Frontend applications need to discover server-side auth configuration to dynamically render appropriate login buttons (email/password, Google, GitHub, etc.) without hardcoding provider lists.

## Changes

### Protocol Layer (`packages/spec/src/api/auth-endpoints.zod.ts`)
- Added `AuthProviderInfoSchema` - public OAuth provider metadata (id, name, enabled)
- Added `EmailPasswordConfigPublicSchema` - email/password auth settings
- Added `AuthFeaturesConfigSchema` - feature flags (2FA, passkeys, magic link, organization)
- Added `GetAuthConfigResponseSchema` - complete config discovery response
- All sensitive fields (clientSecret, secret) excluded by design

### Backend (`packages/plugins/plugin-auth/`)
- Added `AuthManager.getPublicConfig()` - extracts safe config from internal state
  - Filters disabled providers
  - Maps provider IDs to friendly names (google → Google)
  - Returns only non-sensitive configuration
- Registered `GET /api/v1/auth/config` endpoint in `AuthPlugin`
  - Returns standard JSON envelope format
  - Includes error handling

### Client SDK (`packages/client/src/index.ts`)
- Added `client.auth.getConfig()` method
- Exported config types: `GetAuthConfigResponse`, `AuthProviderInfo`, etc.

### Tests
- Comprehensive test coverage for `getPublicConfig()`
- Validates sensitive data exclusion
- Tests provider filtering and name mapping
- Verifies default values

## Usage Example

```typescript
// Frontend discovers available auth methods
const client = new ObjectStackClient({ baseUrl: window.location.origin });
const config = await client.auth.getConfig();

// Dynamically render social login buttons
config.socialProviders.forEach(provider => {
  renderButton({
    label: `Login with ${provider.name}`,
    onClick: () => window.location.href = `/api/v1/auth/authorize/${provider.id}`
  });
});
```

## Response Format

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "emailPassword": {
      "enabled": true,
      "disableSignUp": false,
      "requireEmailVerification": false
    },
    "socialProviders": [
      { "id": "google", "name": "Google", "enabled": true },
      { "id": "github", "name": "GitHub", "enabled": true }
    ],
    "features": {
      "twoFactor": true,
      "passkeys": false,
      "magicLink": false,
      "organization": true
    }
  }
}
```
